# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: bleep64-key-word-4-wraps
why: The key is CRYPTO_KEYBYTES = 16 bytes = 4 words (key[0..3]), but the IV setup reads key[4], a fifth word past the
why: key (AddressSanitizer heap-buffer-overflow, CI run 45610244076): every output depended on whatever followed the key
why: in memory, so the same key/nonce/message encrypted differently on different platforms (macOS decrypt failure).
why: The rest of the setup uses the key words cyclically (key[0], key[1], key[2], key[3], key[0], key[1]); the patch
why: reads word 4 mod 4 = key[0], the same cycle. No KATs exist, so this is a NextSSL choice (tier stays unverified).
file: upstream/ref/encrypt.c
count: 1
find:   t  = key[0] * (iv[0] + key[4]);
replace:   t  = key[0] * (iv[0] + key[0]);
